{
  "dom_id": "step-q181729",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Complete the following reasoning about the set $S=(-\\infty ,1):$\n\nThe value $1$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because {{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if \n\n- ${x}_{max}\\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nIn our case, the value $1$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because $1\\notin S.$",
